
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
DA = DB [00]
DB = DC [01]
DE = DA [02]
F,A,C are collinear [03]
EF ⟂ AC [04]
EG ⟂ AB [05]
B,A,G are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. F,A,C are collinear [03] & EF ⟂ AC [04] ⇒  FE ⟂ FA [07]
002. FE ⟂ FA [07] & EG ⟂ AB [05] ⇒  ∠FEG = ∠FAB [08]
003. F,A,C are collinear [03] & ∠FEG = ∠FAB [08] ⇒  ∠EFA = ∠(EG-BA) [09]
004. DA = DB [00] & DE = DA [02] & DB = DC [01] ⇒  B,E,A,C are concyclic [10]
005. B,E,A,C are concyclic [10] ⇒  ∠ABE = ∠ACE [11]
006. B,E,A,C are concyclic [10] ⇒  ∠EAB = ∠ECB [12]
007. F,A,C are collinear [03] & ∠ACE = ∠ABE [11] ⇒  ∠(FA-EC) = ∠ABE [13]
008. ∠EFA = ∠(EG-BA) [09] & ∠(FA-EC) = ∠ABE [13] ⇒  ∠FEG = ∠CEB [14]
009. F,A,C are collinear [03] & B,A,G are collinear [06] & ∠FEG = ∠FAB [08] ⇒  ∠EFA = ∠EGA [15]
010. ∠EFA = ∠EGA [15] ⇒  F,E,A,G are concyclic [16]
011. F,E,A,G are concyclic [16] ⇒  ∠FEA = ∠FGA [17]
012. ∠EAB = ∠ECB [12] & ∠FEA = ∠FGA [17] & B,A,G are collinear [06] ⇒  ∠EFG = ∠ECB [18]
013. ∠FEG = ∠CEB [14] & ∠EFG = ∠ECB [18] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ΔEFG is similar to ΔECB
==========================
